arch c_sage
name Old jeweler
msg
@match VALLEYNOY
I would not call it a town anymore, friend. Not truly.
I found VALLEYNOY by accident, wandering south of Navar where the maps grow uncertain. There were no roads leading in, only broken stone half-swallowed by the land. Towers lay collapsed as if pressed flat by an unseen hand, and the air felt? thin, as though something had been taken from it.
Whatever HAPPENED here was not war. No siege leaves ruins like these.

@match HAPPENED
If I knew, I would not sleep so poorly.
There are scorch marks without fire, melted metal without heat. Tools fused into walls. Armor lying empty, as if the people simply stepped out of it. I believe VALLEYNOY was a place of ARTIFICERS, folk who bent magic into steel and stone.
Something went wrong. Something very wrong.

@match ARTIFICERS
Yes. Their work is everywhere, even now.
You can still find fragments of enchanted gear buried in the rubble, humming softly when the wind is right. I think they were reaching for something beyond their skill?trying to bind forces that should not be tethered.
The TOWERS were not just buildings. They were instruments.

@match TOWERS
I saw its remains from a distance before I dared enter.
A foundation so deep it vanishes into darkness, and above it? nothing. As if the sky itself tore the rest away. Some say they were attempting to recreate the NAVARIAN TOWER to be like a chain fixed between worlds.
Standing near it made my teeth ache.
And then there's talk of the old LIBRARY...

@match LIBRARY
Ah. The LIBRARY is the reason I lingered as long as I did.
On the northern edge of the ruins sits the ruined foundation of a lost structure,
I have often seen examples wherecases are crushed, but not destroyed, and
ARTIFICERS records were not kept lightly.

@match RECORDS
I am certain there are sealed vaults beneath the rubble. The ground sounds hollow when struck. I lacked the tools, and perhaps the courage, to go further.
If you intend to DIG there, be warned: wards may still linger, confused and hungry.

@match DIG
You have the right idea.
Where the soil is loose,  That is where I would start were I a braver soul. Knowledge buried in VALLEYNOY may yet be intact? or cursed.
Either way, it is not meant to stay forgotten forever.

@match *
You look like someone chasing answers.
Like myself, you seem to have found VALLEYNOY.
endmsg
